    {
      "id": "PKri",
      "code_hash": "5ab237c46aee303381f42e1ba0e419fd",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/html": "<div style='display: flex;flex: 1;flex-direction: column;justify-content: flex-start;align-items: normal;flex-wrap: nowrap;gap: 0.5rem'><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Massive, spin-averaged squared matrix element</strong> \u2014 all three polarization choices give the same result.</span></span><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap; margin: 0;\">-2\u00b7<span style=\"color: rgb(128, 128, 128)\">(</span>-ee\u2074\u00b7t\u00b7u\u00b3+7\u00b7ee\u2074\u00b7Me\u00b2\u00b7t\u00b7u\u00b2+7\u00b7ee\u2074\u00b7Me\u00b2\u00b7t\u00b2\u00b7u+ee\u2074\u00b7Me\u00b2\u00b7t\u00b3+ee\u2074\u00b7Me\u00b2\u00b7u\u00b3\n    -14\u00b7ee\u2074\u00b7Me\u2074\u00b7t\u00b7u-3\u00b7ee\u2074\u00b7Me\u2074\u00b7t\u00b2-3\u00b7ee\u2074\u00b7Me\u2074\u00b7u\u00b2+6\u00b7ee\u2074\u00b7Me\u2078-ee\u2074\u00b7t\u00b3\u00b7u\n<span style=\"color: rgb(128, 128, 128)\">)</span>/<span style=\"color: rgb(128, 128, 128)\">(</span><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">(</span>t-Me\u00b2<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">)</span>\u00b2\u00b7<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">(</span>-u+Me\u00b2<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">)</span>\u00b2<span style=\"color: rgb(128, 128, 128)\">)</span></div></div>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "Xref",
      "code_hash": "2a34a6246699122f5a96976d8592347b",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"identical-photons-and-angular-acceptance\">Identical photons and angular acceptance</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Let <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(c=\\cos\\theta||)</marimo-tex> and accept events with <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(|c|&lt;C&lt;1||)</marimo-tex>. The labeled massless\nangular density is <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\alpha^2(1+c^2)/[s(1-c^2)]||)</marimo-tex>. Integrating it over the\nfull sphere counts both photon assignments; the event rate includes <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(1/2!||)</marimo-tex>.\nEquivalently, select the forward photon and integrate over <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(0&lt;c&lt;C||)</marimo-tex>.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><code>Kinematics.flux</code> and <code>two_body_phase_space</code> supply the flux and measure.\nSymbolica integrates the rational angular distribution. The massless result,\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\sigma=2\\pi\\alpha^2[2\\operatorname{atanh}C-C]/s||)</marimo-tex>, also matches\n<a href=\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-ex/0409058\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">DELPHI's Born formula, Eq. (2)</a>.\nFor a massive electron, <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\beta=\\sqrt{1-4m_e^2/s}||)</marimo-tex> is the incoming CM speed.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "SFPL",
      "code_hash": "5f1e8133acb2d8dc44af74472e216193",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/html": "<div style='display: flex;flex: 1;flex-direction: column;justify-content: flex-start;align-items: normal;flex-wrap: nowrap;gap: 0.5rem'><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Massless labeled angular density</strong></span></span><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap; margin: 0;\">-<span style=\"color: rgb(128, 128, 128)\">(</span>cos_theta\u00b2\u00b7alpha\u00b2+alpha\u00b2<span style=\"color: rgb(128, 128, 128)\">)</span>/<span style=\"color: rgb(128, 128, 128)\">(</span>s\u00b7<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">(</span>-1+cos_theta<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">)</span>\u00b7<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">(</span>1+cos_theta<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">)</span><span style=\"color: rgb(128, 128, 128)\">)</span></div><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Massless event cross section with angular cut</strong></span></span><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap; margin: 0;\">-2\u00b7<span style=\"color: rgb(128, 128, 128)\">(</span><span style=\"color: rgb(205, 0, 205)\">\ud835\udf0b</span>\u00b7alpha\u00b2\u00b7cutoff-2\u00b7<span style=\"color: rgb(205, 0, 205)\">\ud835\udf0b</span>\u00b7alpha\u00b2\u00b7<span style=\"color: rgb(205, 0, 205)\">atanh</span><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">(</span>cutoff<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">)</span><span style=\"color: rgb(128, 128, 128)\">)</span>/s</div><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Massive event cross section with angular cut</strong></span></span><div style=\"white-space: pre-wrap; margin: 0;\">-2\u00b7<span style=\"color: rgb(205, 0, 205)\">\ud835\udf0b</span>\u00b7alpha\u00b2\n    \u00b7<span style=\"color: rgb(128, 128, 128)\">(</span>-2\u00b7cutoff\u00b7beta+2\u00b7cutoff\u00b7beta\u00b3-cutoff\u00b7beta\u2075+3\u00b7<span style=\"color: rgb(205, 0, 205)\">atanh</span><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">(</span>cutoff\u00b7beta<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">)</span>\n        -3\u00b7cutoff\u00b2\u00b7beta\u00b2\u00b7<span style=\"color: rgb(205, 0, 205)\">atanh</span><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">(</span>cutoff\u00b7beta<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">)</span>+cutoff\u00b2\u00b7beta\u2076\u00b7<span style=\"color: rgb(205, 0, 205)\">atanh</span><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">(</span>cutoff\u00b7beta<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">)</span>\n        +cutoff\u00b3\u00b7beta\u00b3-beta\u2074\u00b7<span style=\"color: rgb(205, 0, 205)\">atanh</span><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">(</span>cutoff\u00b7beta<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">)</span>\n    <span style=\"color: rgb(128, 128, 128)\">)</span>/<span style=\"color: rgb(128, 128, 128)\">(</span>s\u00b7beta\u00b2\u00b7<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">(</span>-1+cutoff\u00b7beta<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">)</span>\u00b7<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">(</span>1+cutoff\u00b7beta<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 95, 175)\">)</span><span style=\"color: rgb(128, 128, 128)\">)</span></div></div>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
